# Prefer CLI for scaffolding

Use official CLI commands whenever they exist. Do not hand-write generated project trees, `pubspec.yaml` skeletons, platform folders, or plugin/package boilerplate.

## Flutter / Dart in this repo

Create packages, plugins, and apps with `flutter create` (or `dart create` when Flutter is not required). Run commands from the correct parent directory.

```bash
# SDK Dart/Flutter package (e.g. thawani_models, networking)
cd sdk
flutter create --template=package <package_name>

# SDK plugin (only if a native plugin is actually needed)
cd sdk
flutter create --template=plugin <plugin_name>

# Explorer app
cd apps
flutter create explorer
```

After CLI scaffold, only then edit generated files (path dependencies, flavors, DI, analysis options).

## Other CLIs

Same rule outside Flutter: `git`, `dart`, `flutter pub`, `melos`, and similar tools beat recreating their output by hand.

## Do not

- Copy-paste a `lib/`, `android/`, `ios/`, or `test/` tree into a new package/app
- Invent `pubspec.yaml` from memory when `flutter create` would produce it
- Skip CLI flags that the task needs (`--template`, `--platforms`, `--org`, etc.)
